.\" Title: vrc-spawn-in
.\" Author: vrc contributors
.\" Manual section: 1
.\"
.TH VRC\-SPAWN\-IN 1 "2025" "vrc" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
vrc\-spawn\-in \- spawn a new command inside a running vrc instance

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vrc
\fBspawn\-in\fR \fIPID\fR \fICMD\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Spawn a new command inside an already-running vrc instance. The new command gets its own virtual terminal (VTTY) with independent scrollback, and is added to the instance's command list visible via \fBvrc list\fR.

Connects to the target instance's UDS control socket at \fB~/.local/share/vrc/control\-{pid}.sock\fR and sends the spawn request.

The spawned command uses the instance's default VTTY settings (rows, cols, TERM value) unless overridden in the configuration. Environment variables from the config are passed to the new command.

This is the UDS equivalent of vrw's \fBvrw spawn\fR command.

.SH ARGUMENTS

.TP
.B PID
OS process ID of the target vrc instance.

.TP
.B CMD
The command to run (e.g., \fBhtop\fR, \fBvim\fR, \fB./my-script.sh\fR).

.TP
.B ARGS...
Additional arguments to pass to the command.

.SH EXAMPLES

.PP
Spawn htop in a running instance:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc spawn\-in 12345 htop\fR
Spawned command cmd_abc (PID 5678) in instance 12345
.fi
.RE

.PP
Spawn a script with arguments:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc spawn\-in 12345 ./build.sh \-\-release \-\-verbose\fR
Spawned command cmd_def (PID 5679) in instance 12345
.fi
.RE

.PP
Spawn vim to edit a file:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc spawn\-in 12345 vim /path/to/file.rs\fR
Spawned command cmd_ghi (PID 5680) in instance 12345
.fi
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS

.TP
.B 0
Command spawned successfully.

.TP
.B 1
Error (instance not found, spawn failed, etc.).

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vrc (1),
.BR vrc\-list (1),
.BR vrc\-kill (1),
.BR vrc\-freeze (1)
